        "title": "CLI ad banner refactor: choice-ad-banner.tsx renamed to ad-banner.tsx",
        "summary": "cli/src/components/choice-ad-banner.tsx renamed to cli/src/components/ad-banner.tsx. SingleAdBanner exported for chat (cli/src/chat.tsx), ChoiceAdBanner for waiting room (cli/src/components/waiting-room-screen.tsx). AD_CARD_HEIGHT replaces CHOICE_AD_BANNER_HEIGHT. Chat renders ads?.[0] via SingleAdBanner instead of full ads array via ChoiceAdBanner.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:24:19.889Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you chat in the Freebuffer waiting room, you will now see only the single top-sponsored banner ad instead of the full set, and the chat view collapses any extra ad slots that used to stack. Under the hood the program that paints that banner was split into two: one part handles the waiting-room view you see today (keeping its existing height and padding), and the other handles the single banner shown mid-conversation, so the two screens no longer share the same code. Everything you see looks the same as before, but the pieces behind the screen were rearranged to make that one difference.",
